ocal initialization summary for later review.",featurePreviewScope:"Feature switches use the existing configuration interfaces and do not change permissions, authorization, edition capabilities, or business data."},initializationRecord:{title:"Local initialization summary",status:"Initialization status",completed:"Local initialization completed; available for review",completedAt:"Completed at",roles:"Current role configuration",roleCount:"{count} total",defaultsScope:"The content below reads current System Settings. The initialization summary only records completion and the configuration overview at that time.",roleDetails:"Current role configuration",fieldDetails:"Default field names",costDetails:"Default cost adjustments",flowDetails:"Project Flow stages and sample tasks",templateDetails:"Template backup import status",configurationCheckDetails:"Configuration check status",scope:"This summary records completion and a configuration overview only. Reopening the wizard uses current System Settings.",missingTitle:"Completion marker found without an initialization summary",missingDescription:"This is a compatibility state from the earlier wizard. It is not reset automatically; complete the wizard again to create a local summary, or use the development reset."},completion:{success:"The local wizard completion marker and initialization summary were saved. Future entries from System Settings can review them.",failed:"The browser-local completion marker and initialization summary could not be saved. Check browser storage permissions."},reset:{title:"Development testing",description:"Local development / testing only. This clears only the wizard completion state and initialization summary in this browser; it does not delete IndexedDB, projects or other business data.",confirmTitle:"Reset local initialization status?",confirmMessage:"This only removes the wizard completion marker and local initialization summary from this browser and returns the flow to step 1. It does not clear IndexedDB, projects, checklists, quotations, settlement, shipment, recycle, products, customers, fonts, templates, export files or cloud data.",success:"The wizard completion marker and local initialization summary were cleared. You can test again from step 1.",failed:"The wizard completion marker and local initialization summary could not be cleared. Check browser storage permissions."},firstRun:{title:"Set up your workspace",subtitle:"A short local initialization for this device. Existing workspaces are adopted without rewriting their labels or business configuration.",progress:"Step {current} of {total}",actions:{back:"Back",next:"Continue",complete:"Complete setup",returnToInitialization:"Return to initialization"},steps:{language:"Language",method:"Setup method",legal:"Terms and local data",workspace:"Workspace and administrator",flow:"Flow direction",options:"Core options",teamCode:"Team code",review:"Review and complete"},language:{title:"Choose your language",prompt:"This language controls the wizard now. The final selection is saved as the workspace initialization language when setup is completed.",zhCN:"简体中文",en:"English"},method:{title:"How do you want to start?",restore:"Restore from backup",team:"Join an existing team",newLocal:"New local setup",restoreDescription:"Use an existing LumePilot backup to restore this device. You will not create a new administrator.",teamDescription:"Use a Team Code to configure this device for an existing team, then sign in with your team account.",newLocalDescription:"Create a new workspace on this device.",unavailable:"Not available yet",restoreOpening:"Opening recovery…",restoreFailed:"The recovery entry could not be opened. Try again.",required:"Choose an available setup method to continue. For a new local workspace, a system administrator can configure Cloud later in System Settings > Data & Sync; joining an existing team is only part of the first-run Team setup."},legal:{title:"Review the local-data notices",teamTitle:"Review the notices for joining your team",agreementTitle:"User Agreement",agreementBody:"This placeholder confirms that you are using LumePilot for your own local workspace. A complete agreement will be provided before any future service terms are introduced.",teamAgreementBody:"This placeholder confirms that you are using LumePilot to access a team workspace. A complete agreement will be provided before any future service terms are introduced.",privacyTitle:"Privacy Policy",privacyBody:"This placeholder explains the current local product scope. It is not a promise about future cloud services.",teamPrivacyBody:"This placeholder explains the current product scope when this device is configured for an existing team.",localDataTitle:"Local Data Storage Notice",localDataBody:"LumePilot currently uses local data storage as its primary mode. When cloud services are not enabled, projects and business data remain on this device.",acceptAgreement:"I have read the User Agreement placeholder.",acceptPrivacy:"I have read the Privacy Policy placeholder.",acceptLocalData:"I understand the Local Data Storage Notice.",teamLocalDataNote:"Your Team Code configures this device for an existing team. Team sign-in happens after setup; this notice does not require a separate confirmation here.",required:"Please confirm all three notices before continuing."},teamCode:{title:"Join your team",prompt:"Enter the Member Join Code provided by your administrator. Existing Team Codes are also supported.",label:"Member Join Code",placeholder:"Paste the code from your administrator",scan:"Scan QR code",scanning:"Scan the team code QR code",closeScanner:"Close scanner",scannerDesktopUnavailable:"QR scanning is not available in this desktop client. Paste the Member Join Code instead.",scannerUnsupported:"QR scanning is not available here. Paste the Member Join Code instead.",scannerPermissionDenied:"Camera access was not allowed. Paste the Member Join Code instead.",scannerFailed:"The QR code could not be read. Paste the Member Join Code instead.",scannerNoDetection:"No Member Join Code was detected. Check the code and try again.",manualFallback:"You can paste the Member Join Code manually.",validating:"Checking the team…",verified:"Team verified:",errors:{invalid:"This Member Join Code is not valid. Check the code and try again.",endpointUnreachable:"The team could not be reached. Check your connection and try again.",protocolIncompatible:"This Member Join Code is not compatible with this version of LumePilot.",workspaceNotFound:"The team could not be found. Check the code and try again.",descriptorMismatch:"The Member Join Code does not match the team target.",remoteValidationFailed:"The team could not be verified right now. Try again later."}},workspace:{title:"Name the workspace and create its local administrator",nameLabel:"Workspace name",optional:"Optional",namePlaceholder:"e.g. North Star Lighting Studio",adminTitle:"Local administrator",loginLabel:"Login name",loginPlaceholder:"Choose a local login name",displayLabel:"Display name",displayOptional:"Optional; defaults to the login name",displayPlaceholder:"Optional display name",passwordLabel:"Password",confirmLabel:"Confirm password",passwordPlaceholder:"Required local password",confirmPlaceholder:"Enter the password again",note:"This local administrator is only for LumePilot on the current device. It is not a cloud account."},flow:{title:"Choose a project flow direction",prompt:"Project Flow is required in this version. Choose the default business direction for new project work.",lighting:"Lighting business",lightingDescription:"Lighting design, selection, quotation and fulfillment.",furniture:"Furniture business",furnitureDescription:"Furniture supply, delivery, installation and settlement.",required:"Choose one flow direction to continue."},options:{title:"Choose the core options",productCode:"Product Code",productCodeDescription:"Keep the product code field available in the quote workspace.",designer:"Designer Selection",designerDescription:"Enable the designer selection checklist.",candidates:"Main Checklist Multi Quote Candidates",candidatesDescription:"Allow multiple quote candidates before signing.",on:"On",off:"Off"},review:{title:"Review and complete setup",locale:"Initialization language",method:"Setup method",newLocal:"New local setup",team:"Join an existing team",teamTarget:"Team",workspace:"Workspace name",admin:"Local administrator",flow:"Flow direction",terms:"Legal and local-data notices",confirmed:"Confirmed",empty:"Not entered",completeNote:"Complete writes the workspace defaults and credentials together. The lifecycle record is written last.",teamCompleteNote:"Complete saves this device’s Team Code configuration. No member account is created and no member session starts here; the team sign-in screen opens next."},initializing:"Completing setup…",setupComplete:"Setup complete. Continue to local sign-in.",errors:{required:"This field is required.",invalidLogin:"Use a non-empty login name without spaces or control characters.",password:"Password does not meet the current local password policy.",mismatch:"Passwords do not match.",method:"This setup method is not available yet.",legal:"Confirm all required notices before continuing.",legalTeam:"Confirm the User Agreement and Privacy Policy before continuing.",flow:"Choose a flow direction before continuing.",restoreReturnFailed:"LumePilot could not return to initialization. Keep this recovery screen open and try again.",failed:"Setup could not be completed. No final initialization state was recorded. Please try again."}}},Yct={"setup-wizard-overview":{purpose:"Choose how this device starts and understand what must finish before you enter a workspace.",entry:"An uninitialized device opens the Setup Wizard at startup. Sign in normally on a device with an existing workspace. Use MENU → System Settings for everyday configuration; do not clear data to restart setup.",prerequisites:"Check whether the device holds data you need to keep. New local setup requires a local administrator account. Team setup needs a valid Team Code, a team account and network access. Restore requires a supported desktop client and a valid backup.",steps:{1:"Choose Simplified Chinese or English, then select New local setup, Join an existing team, or Restore from backup.",2:"For New local setup, read the terms, privacy and local-data notices and complete the required acknowledgements. Enter the workspace and administrator details. The workspace display name is optional; the login name and both password entries must pass the displayed checks.",3:"Choose a flow direction and review the core options, including product codes, designer selection checklists and multiple main quotation candidates. Review and complete setup, then sign in with the local administrator you created.",4:"For Join an existing team, complete the required acknowledgements and enter the Team Code supplied by your administrator. Scan only if the device offers that option. Wait for remote validation, then review and finish device configuration.",5:"Follow the team sign-in or join prompts. Wait for initial synchronization and readiness. Resolve any pending team foundation, business-data or resource notice before using the affected features.",6:"For Restore from backup, open the dedicated recovery page, select the backup, complete its checks and confirm recovery as instructed. Continue only after success is reported. Cancelling, returning or failing to open recovery does not complete a restore."},result:"A new local workspace becomes accessible through local sign-in. Team configuration prepares the device for team entry; team identity and initial synchronization are still required. After a successful restore, follow its result to enter the restored workspace.",notes:{1:"A local administrator, a team member and a workspace owner are different identities. Creating a local administrator does not grant team ownership. Settings visibility and editing depend on the signed-in account’s permissions.",2:"Recovery requires desktop recovery support and backup compatibility checks. A normal web page cannot replace native recovery. Review the recovery warnings about existing data and Cloud binding before proceeding.",3:"Team capabilities are available only after the current identity, connection status and sync readiness checks pass. For team settings and custom roles saved by an administrator, confirm the update on member devices. When using the furniture workflow preset, review the project flow tasks actually created."}},"project-lifecycle":{purpose:"Create a project, find its home page and distinguish progress tracking from actual quotation, ordering and delivery actions.",entry:"Use New Project from Workspace or MENU → Project List. Enter an existing project from Project List to reach its home page, project profile, Project Flow and available checklist entries.",prerequisites:"Sign in with permission to create or view the project. Team members also need access to that project. Use the valid project categories and member options offered by the current form.",steps:{1:"Choose New Project, enter a project name and select a valid project category. Add location, customer, contact and project-member details as needed. Check the form’s required-field messages.",2:"Submit and wait for the result. If the project was created but flow initialization failed, keep that project and use the offered retry action. Do not create another project to repeat the same attempt.",3:"Enter the project from Project List. Review its home page, then check customer, address and contact inputs in the project profile. Save changes only when your account has edit access.",4:"Open Project Flow to inspect stages and tasks. Use the available views to inspect task details, assignees, planned dates and linked business entries.",5:"Update ordinary process tasks to reflect actual progress or responsibility. For tasks linked to checklists, formal quotes, fulfillment or settlement, open the relevant business panel and perform the real action there.",6:"Return to the project home page or Project Flow to check the result. To enter products or prepare a quote, open the project’s checklists and use actions allowed for the checklist type and current state."},result:"The project connects its profile, checklists and process records. Project Flow shows progress and business links; actual quotation, signing, ordering, shipment and settlement facts come from the corresponding business actions.",notes:{1:"Completing a task does not automatically generate a formal quote, sign a checklist, place an order, ship goods or confirm receipt. Linked business actions remain subject to their own prerequisites.",2:"Project Flow may be disabled by configuration. Project scope and editing also depend on permissions. Ask an administrator to check missing or read-only entries instead of repeatedly creating projects.",3:"When using the furniture preset, review the project flow tasks actually created; a preset name alone does not prove them. Reading Help does not change existing projects or protected business snapshots."}},"formal-quote-and-signing":{purpose:"Generate a formal customer quote, mark it as quoted and sign in the correct order, without treating a draft, preview or completed task as signing evidence.",entry:"Open the product workspace from the project checklist and choose Generate Quotation. After generation, use that checklist’s formal quotation panel in Project Flow to review revisions, mark as quoted and sign.",prerequisites:"An applicable project checklist must exist with saved products and quotation inputs, plus an available customer quotation template. Your account needs quotation and checklist-action permissions. The checklist must satisfy the current signing conditions.",steps:{1:"Open the intended checklist. Review products, quantities, customer-facing prices and quotation inputs, then save your edits. Confirm the checklist or quotation candidate you are working on.",2:"Choose Generate Quotation, enter preflight and preview, select the customer quotation template and inspect its customer-facing content. Opening a preview alone does not finish formal generation.",3:"Use PDF download in the formal customer quotation flow and handle its preflight and save prompts. This flow establishes a Quote Revision and QVS1 verification information. If it reports failure, check the page result before treating a file or preview as success.",4:"Open the checklist’s formal quotation panel in Project Flow. Check its revision and Quotation Generated status, then choose Mark as quoted. This records quotation status; it does not sign the checklist.",5:"Sign against the content confirmed with the customer. If the formal revision is stale, review the changes first. Explicitly confirm regeneration when prompted, or return to formal generation and inspect the new revision before signing.",6:"Check the signed status and referenced quotation revision. Use the corresponding formal revision or signed snapshot when viewing or exporting that historical quote."},result:"The formal revision records the customer quotation and template at generation time. QVS1 verifies quotation content. Signing requires quoted status, references a valid formal revision and protects the corresponding historical snapshots.",notes:{1:"Saving a checklist, exporting Excel separately, downloading an existing revision file or manually completing a Generate Quotation task cannot replace formal generation. Initial signing cannot invent a missing formal revision.",2:"Edits after quotation can make a revision stale. Explicitly confirmed regeneration creates a new formal revision; it does not overwrite the old quote or mean that signing alone creates verification information.",3:"Ordinary editing is restricted after signing. Later template or default-setting changes do not rewrite historical quotes. Reversing a signature also depends on downstream business conditions; this article does not bypass those protections."}},"app-basics-navigation":{purpose:"Find everyday business entries and distinguish navigation, draft editing and committed changes.",entry:"After sign-in, start at the workspace overview. Use MENU at the upper left to switch modules, or Project List to enter a specific project.",prerequisites:"The device is initialized, you are signed in, and your account can access the required module and project.",steps:{1:"From the overview, choose New Project or view all projects. For existing work, open Project List and locate the project first.",2:"Enter the project home page, then open its profile, Project Flow, checklists or documents. Check the project name before editing.",3:"For work across projects, open MENU and choose an available module such as Customer Library, Product Library, Shipment Management, Product Recycling Library or After-sales. Open System Settings for configuration.",4:"After editing a form or sheet, use its Save, Submit or Confirm action and check the result. Cancel discards unsubmitted edits in that panel. Returning or switching modules is not a universal save action.",5:"On narrow screens, open details from a list and use Back to return. Row editing may use a bottom sheet. Both desktop tables or split views and narrow layouts require their own save confirmation."},result:"You reach the intended project or module. Only successfully committed actions create business data.",notes:{1:"For missing, read-only or denied entries, check permissions, project scope and module settings. A planned entry does not mean the feature is available.",2:"Viewing, searching, filtering and expanding rows usually change presentation only. Resolve unsaved edits before leaving. If saving fails, keep the input and inspect the error rather than creating duplicate records."}},"customer-library-basics":{purpose:"Maintain customers and contacts centrally and select the right customer for a project.",entry:"MENU → Customer Library. Customer selection and binding are available in project creation and the project profile.",prerequisites:"Viewing requires customer access. Creating, editing and maintaining contact methods require the corresponding permissions, and project binding requires the relevant project access.",steps:{1:"Search the library and check the customer name, organization and contacts. Similar names do not establish that two records are the same customer.",2:"Choose Add Customer, enter the required customer name and add organization, city, advisor, notes and contact methods as needed, then save. Use Edit for an existing customer. Cancel does not submit the current form draft.",3:"After success, review the customer details. If saving reports an error, search for the customer and inspect its contacts before retrying so that you do not create duplicates.",4:"In New Project or the project profile, search for and select the customer. Check the binding and project contact inputs, then submit. Review customer master data and project contact inputs separately.",5:"With permission, expand the customer’s historical quotation records and inspect products and sources. Use them as a reference to quotations actually recorded for that customer."},result:"The customer becomes available for later project selection. The project binds to that customer, while historical formal quotations retain their original business content.",notes:{1:"Customer quotation history is not a complete archive of every project, file or agreed price. No record does not prove there was no quotation. Reading this history also requires separate permission.",2:"Changing customer master data does not re-sign or overwrite old quote snapshots. Historical prices do not replace a fresh project quotation review. Check the source project and formal revision when a record differs."}},"product-library-basics":{purpose:"Keep reusable product details and valid cost references to reduce repeated entry.",entry:"MENU → Product Library. Find or select the brand, then locate the product.",prerequisites:"Product-library viewing and maintenance need their corresponding permissions. Costs and cost history also require sensitive-cost access. Have the brand and real product model ready.",steps:{1:"Search and check brand, real model and specification. Identity is the brand-plus-model combination; surrounding spaces and letter case do not create a different product identity.",2:"To add a product, select a valid brand and enter its name, real model, unit and required specifications. If the brand is missing, create it through the permitted brand-management entry first.",3:"When editing, verify the target record, change the required details and save. Cancel does not submit the current form draft. For a duplicate-identity warning, return to the existing record.",4:"With cost access, inspect current cost and recent valid cost history, including source and date. Zero is not a valid cost update and does not replace an existing valid nonzero cost.",5:"When selecting a library product into a checklist, check the populated model, quantity and cost, then save the checklist. Review existing rows in their own checklist rather than assuming a library change updated them."},result:"Product master data supports later lookup and entry. Cost history retains valid cost sources; formal business records keep their own quotation or execution snapshots.",notes:{1:"The real model and customer-facing product code are different. Do not change product identity just to change customer-facing text.",2:"Changing library names or costs must not rewrite formal historical quotes, signing evidence or order execution snapshots. Use the owning business workflow to correct current work.",3:"A blank cost may mean restricted access or no valid record. Check permissions and source history instead of using zero as a confirmed purchasing cost."}},"checklist-config-fields":{purpose:"Configure checklist inputs and customer output without confusing internal working fields with customer-visible content.",entry:"MENU → System Settings → Projects & Checklists → Checklist & Cost Settings → Fields.",prerequisites:"Viewing requires checklist-configuration access; editing and saving require management permission. Confirm that you are changing defaults rather than a historical quotation.",steps:{1:"Locate the field and check whether it is a system or custom field. Review protected, computed and internal-information indicators.",2:"To add a field, choose Add Field, enter a display name, select an allowed input type and quotation visibility, then confirm. The system assigns a stable identity.",3:"Configure enablement, workspace display, collapsed display and ordering as needed. Enablement controls availability; workspace display controls presentation. Renaming does not replace the field identity.",4:"Review Quote Visible separately. Quote visibility does not mean workspace visibility: an editable workspace field may be hidden from customers, and a disabled field cannot be forced into output simply by selecting Quote Visible.",5:"Save the configuration and check success, then inspect an applicable checklist. Cancelling an edit panel discards that panel’s draft only; resolve any unsaved configuration before leaving."},result:"The saved configuration is used by applicable checklists. Customer output remains subject to template and safe-field rules, and renaming does not change historical field identity.",notes:{1:"Protected, computed, image and sensitive internal fields may lock type, deletion or output controls. This is not a failed save; do not bypass those controls.",2:"Deleting a custom field requires the displayed confirmation and does not erase its historical meaning. Default changes do not rewrite formal quotation or signed snapshots.",3:"For a missing working field, check enablement, workspace display, collapsed state and permissions. For missing customer output, also check Quote Visible and the template."}},"cost-adjustment-config":{purpose:"Maintain default cost increases and deductions for consistent entry in business workspaces.",entry:"MENU → System Settings → Projects & Checklists → Checklist & Cost Settings → Cost.",prerequisites:"Checklist-configuration permissions control viewing and editing. Sensitive costs need the corresponding viewing permission. Default rule definitions and actual project amounts are separate data.",steps:{1:"Choose the increase or deduction group and inspect existing entries before adding another adjustment for the same purpose.",2:"Add a custom entry or edit an existing one. Enter a name and select Amount, Percentage or both where offered. Keep at least one valid method, and review actual amounts and percentages in the applicable business record.",3:"Set enablement, reorder within the group and review customer quotation visibility separately. Permission to view a cost does not mean it may be disclosed to customers.",4:"Save and check the feedback. Draft toggles or ordering changes do not establish a successful save. For errors, check the name, valid value methods and permissions before retrying."},result:"Applicable later checklists can use the saved default adjustments. Historical formal quotations, order execution costs and settlements retain their original evidence.",notes:{1:"Protected system entries are not freely deletable. Disabling a default does not cancel an existing charge or issue a refund.",2:"To change a project’s actual amount, use its checklist or owning business action. Default configuration does not directly rewrite historical amounts.",3:"The read-only calculation mode on Cost Formula is not a custom formula editor. Check permissions and protection notices for locked controls; changing a default adjustment does not change the formula."}},"shipment-rules":{purpose:"Order actual quantities, ship in batches and confirm receipt while retaining execution records at each stage.",entry:"MENU → Shipment Management. Select the project and checklist, then expand a brand, product or batch.",prerequisites:"Ordinary checklists must be signed. After-sales checklists must be confirmed or have a compatible legacy signed record. Appropriate fulfillment permissions, executable products and remaining quantities are required. Settlement, return and reduction checklists are excluded.",steps:{1:"Locate the project and checklist and review remaining orderable products. If none are eligible, check signing or after-sales confirmation in the source business record.",2:"Choose Place Order, select products and enter this order’s quantities, then review execution costs and confirm. Partial orders are supported, but quantities cannot exceed remaining demand. Cancelling the dialog before confirmation creates no confirmed order.",3:"From a confirmed order, choose Ship. Enter batch quantities, shipment time, destination, recipient and logistics details, then create the batch. Manually verify any name, phone and address parsed from pasted text.",4:"Choose the actual destination: project site or company storage. Confirm receipt of a storage batch when it arrives, then use Storage Forwarding to send it to the site. Do not record forwarding as another supplier shipment.",5:"When goods arrive, confirm receipt against the correct batch and check its remaining receivable quantity. Site and storage receipts are separate, and a completed batch cannot be received twice.",6:"For returns or reversal, use the relevant return, order cancellation, shipment cancellation or receipt cancellation entry. If returns, recycle inbound or storage forwarding occupy the record, inspect those links and follow the permitted reversal workflow first.",7:"Review ordered, shipped, received and remaining quantities in the checklist and batch lists. They are separate facts; a single status label does not establish that all stages are complete."},result:"Orders retain product and execution-cost snapshots. Shipments and receipts create separate batch records. Order cost reconciliation does not rewrite the customer’s signed quotation.",notes:{1:"A completed Project Flow task does not place an order, ship goods or confirm receipt. Submit the action through the real business entry.",2:"Cancellation is a guarded reversal, not deletion of history. Do not edit signed rows, repeat receipt or create another batch to bypass occupancy warnings.",3:"Recycle reuse has its own stock allocation and occupies fulfillment demand. Do not count already allocated stock again as purchasing demand."}},"recycle-library-rules":{purpose:"Return products against real business sources and track recycled stock and later reuse.",entry:"Open source selection through the project checklist’s return action. Use MENU → Product Recycling Library for stock, manual inbound and stock actions. Allocate reuse through Shipment Management.",prerequisites:"Project access and the relevant return, recycling or fulfillment permissions are required. Check the source checklist, order, shipment or receipt and its remaining returnable quantity.",steps:{1:"Check the actual source stage: signed before ordering, ordered but unshipped, shipped but unreceived, or confirmed received. Each stage has different quantities and permitted dispositions.",2:"Filter and select real source lines, enter positive return quantities and confirm. The system creates controlled return records and linked rows according to the source stage. Closing unpurchased demand, closing unshipped orders and physically receiving recycled stock have different results.",3:"For received sources, inspect the linked return rows and recycled stock after confirmation. Shipped-but-unreceived returns first record pending recycling quantities; receipt of the corresponding batch executes deferred recycling. Return confirmation alone does not establish inbound stock.",4:"Expand a product in the recycling library to inspect its source lots. A lot is traceable stock from one inbound event. Movements record inbound, consumption and reversing quantity changes; stock summaries are calculated from these records.",5:"For stock without a project-return source, use Manual Inbound. Select a valid brand and enter product name, real model, unit, a positive quantity and required cost and classification tag. Submit and check the source and balance.",6:"For stock actions, choose an allowed purpose such as outbound, factory return or scrap and enter the quantity. To supply a project, allocate matching recycled stock through Shipment Management. Allocation cannot exceed available stock or remaining demand.",7:"Check linked return rows in the checklist, stock balance and reuse occupancy. Cancelling a controlled return row or releasing an allocation requires the corresponding action and occupancy checks; do not add manual inbound to balance it out."},result:"Returns retain their provenance. Actual inbound adds stock lots, while outbound or reuse occupancy reduces availability. Historical customer quotes and original fulfillment snapshots remain intact.",notes:{1:"The same return source cannot be received into stock twice. Reused, consumed or forwarded quantities may block cancellation. Changing a classification tag does not add stock. Enter positive whole numbers for return quantities, not negative values.",2:"After a submission error, inspect linked return rows and stock before retrying. If the source or returnable quantity differs, retain the details for administrator review rather than rewriting the original record.",3:"A return is not a negative quantity entered directly in an after-sales checklist. Use a controlled source. Settled or protected states may also restrict new returns."}},"after-sales-rules":{purpose:"Record later supply and service in a separate after-sales checklist without rewriting the project’s signed quotation.",entry:"Use MENU → After-sales to find work, or create and open after-sales checklists through the project checklist list or the available Project Flow entry.",prerequisites:"The project exists and your account has project scope and after-sales permissions. Follow the current entry’s availability conditions. Prepare the service or supply details; a settlement aggregate is not a product checklist.",steps:{1:"Find the correct project and after-sales checklist. For new work, create an after-sales checklist and check its generated name. Do not edit rows in the original signed main checklist.",2:"Enter this work’s products, quantities and applicable amounts, then save and review. Negative-quantity return rows are not allowed in after-sales checklists; process returns against real sources.",3:"Before confirming after-sales, use Generate Quotation for this checklist, select an applicable after-sales template, complete preflight and preview, and generate the quotation through the formal PDF download flow. Applicable Excel output is also supported, but preview alone or a separate Excel export does not generate a formal quotation.",4:"Once the quotation is generated and its content is agreed, choose Confirm After-sales, read the prompt and submit. Current confirmation records confirmed status without locking the checklist or automatically creating a new formal quotation revision. It differs from ordinary checklist signing.",5:"For actual supply, find the confirmed checklist in Shipment Management and order, ship and receive the remaining quantities. Directory or Project Flow statuses do not replace these actions.",6:"For a return, open an ordinary project checklist that permits controlled return rows and use its return action to check the relevant order, shipment or receipt source. An after-sales checklist cannot be the target for return rows. Stock increases only through actual recycle inbound. For settlement inclusion, inspect the after-sales checklists and amounts allowed by the settlement entry."},result:"The work has its own checklist, confirmation and actual fulfillment records. Adding after-sales does not automatically rewrite the original formal quote, signing snapshot or historical settlement.",notes:{1:"After-sales confirmation is not a signing lock. A historically signed after-sales record still follows its protection rules. Downstream occupancy may also block unconfirmation or reversal.",2:"Customer output follows template and sensitive-information protection. If output fails, inspect both business status and the file result; preview is not proof of completion.",3:"After-sales returns, recycled stock and settlement are linked but separate: confirmation does not automatically receive stock or refund money, and inbound does not change a frozen settlement. Use the owning guarded workflow for historical corrections."}},"role-permission-defaults":{purpose:"Configure the features a role may use, while separating local roles, Team identities and project scope.",entry:"System Settings → Users & Security → Role Permissions. Assign local users through User Management; manage Team membership and project scope through their respective Team and project entries.",prerequisites:"Role management access is required. Creation, editing, deletion and permission assignment have separate checks. Identify whether this is a local or Team workspace first.",steps:{1:"Expand an existing role to inspect its name, description, enabled state and permission groups. Local defaults provide starting roles; customize ordinary roles for actual responsibilities. The protected System Administrator role cannot be edited like an ordinary role.",2:"Choose the create-role action, then set the name, description, enabled state, single-letter badge and colors. The badge letter must pass validation and be unique; its appearance grants no permission. Creation first creates a role record; subsequent edits still need saving.",3:"Search or expand permission groups, select the required capabilities and save the role. Check the feedback. Permission assignment requires its own capability even when name editing is allowed. Save current edits before selecting another role.",4:"To delete, check the role and affected people, then use the deletion confirmation. System roles and protected Team defaults cannot be freely deleted. Deleting a role is not deleting a user or clearing history.",5:"Check assignments and project access in the corresponding people and project entries. Capabilities determine permitted actions; project scope determines which projects they apply to. Ask an administrator to check identity, capabilities and scope for denied, read-only or locked controls."},result:"After a successful save, the role configuration is available to its authorization workflow. Machine-level System Administrator access comes from an authenticated local administrator account; the reserved system role displays all capabilities. Changing a role name or identifier alone cannot grant administrator identity. Team access still depends on valid Team identity and authority.",notes:{1:"A local System Administrator is not automatically the Team Workspace Owner. Owners and ordinary members use Team identity checks; renaming a local role cannot grant ownership.",2:"Team role changes depend on Team authorization and publication state. Local role configuration cannot replace Cloud authority. Cross-device updates of custom roles and system settings are confirmed by the actual result on member devices; a local save does not confirm that other members have updated.",3:"Role changes do not rewrite existing quotation, signing, order, receipt or settlement facts. Historical snapshots and operation attribution remain protected."}},"project-flow-template":{purpose:"Maintain default stages, tasks and categories for new projects without confusing template editing with project progress.",entry:"System Settings → Projects & Checklists → Project Flow Settings. Use General for project categories and Flow for the default template.",prerequisites:"The corresponding view and management permissions are required. Decide whether you need to change the default template or tasks already created inside a project.",steps:{1:"In General, inspect project categories. Add, enable or disable categories as needed. Removal archives a category and retains historical references; it does not erase old projects.",2:"Open Flow and inspect the default stages and tasks. Adjust editable labels, enabled states and order. Protected stage and task identities cannot be freely replaced.",3:"For tasks, configure the supported default assignee roles, planned durations and one-click completion participation. Default roles suggest responsibility; check actual assignees and dates inside each project.",4:"Use the save confirmation control and check the feedback. Switching tabs or changing a draft does not save it. The overall Project Flow switch is currently locked; it is not an editable engine-off control.",5:"When subsequently creating or initializing a project flow, check the generated stages and tasks. Existing projects keep their original template version and task instances. Change actual tasks through the relevant project with the required permission."},result:"Saving creates a new default template version for later flow initialization. It does not bulk-replace existing project tasks or historical events.",notes:{1:"Lighting and furniture offer different workflow presets, rather than separate quotation or stock systems. After choosing the furniture preset, inspect the project tasks actually created instead of treating the preset name as proof.",2:"Project categories are maintainable classifications. They do not grant project access or change quotation calculations. Disabling or archiving a category does not delete historical projects.",3:"Configuration access does not allow rewriting signing, fulfillment or settlement events. Templates, one-click completion settings and ordinary progress updates cannot replace the corresponding business actions."}},"quote-template-editor":{purpose:"Manage formal customer quotation layouts and safe fields, then select the appropriate template before generating a quote.",entry:"Open the product workspace from a project checklist and choose Template management to enter the Customer Quote Template Designer. System Settings → Templates & Assets → Template Settings opens Excel Templates for separate workbooks.",prerequisites:"Template management permission is required. Check the checklist type first; after-sales and ordinary customer quotation templates are managed separately. Prepare the fields, fonts and customer output style you need.",steps:{1:"Select an existing template, or create or duplicate one. Confirm that the target is a customer quotation template and give it an identifiable name.",2:"Adjust page layout, text, blocks, tables and field bindings. Choose fields from the designer’s customer-safe list. Example values in the design preview are for layout checking.",3:"Save the template and check the result, then inspect preview pagination, headings, amounts and fields. Unsaved edits, previewing or exporting configuration cannot replace formal quotation generation.",4:"Use Set as default template for later default selection. This designer uses template selection and default settings rather than the Excel page’s enabled switch. Still check the actual selected template in the formal generation preview.",5:"To transfer configuration, use Export JSON config or Import JSON config. Save the current draft first and read overwrite warnings. Template configuration is not a system backup and does not import projects.",6:"Return to Generate Quotation, select the template and inspect real customer content before formal PDF output. For customer Excel, use the separate quotation Excel output and the quotation workbook configured in System Settings."},result:"Saved templates support later quotation design and selection. A formal Quote Revision retains its generation-time template and content; later default edits must not silently rewrite historical revisions.",notes:{1:"Customer files must exclude costs, suppliers, profits and internal notes. Renaming fields or hiding workspace columns cannot replace customer-safe output restrictions.",2:"The PDF designer and Excel workbooks use different configurations. Importing one does not configure the other. A separate Excel export cannot establish a formal quotation revision.",3:"Opening template management from a signed or ordered checklist still changes future templates only. Use the corresponding revision or signed snapshot for historical quotes; explicitly confirm regeneration when required."}},"settlement-template":{purpose:"Configure the layout and fields of customer settlement documents without changing settlement amounts through a template.",entry:"Open the project’s settlement page and choose Edit Settlement Template to enter the Settlement Template Designer. It is separate from the quotation Excel template list.",prerequisites:"Settlement access is required, plus template management permission for editing. Preview and output need a readable settlement record and must pass the page’s state and output checks.",steps:{1:"Open Edit Settlement Template. Select an existing template or create or duplicate a settlement template, checking its name and target.",2:"Adjust pages, blocks, tables and settlement fields. Available content includes project and customer details, settlement number and date, source checklists, and receivable, paid and remaining amounts. Use the fields offered by the designer.",3:"Save and preview. Check amount labels, checklist detail, pagination and customer-visible information. Set a default if needed, and distinguish the default from the current selection.",4:"Return to settlement output, inspect the selected template and settlement content, then save the PDF. Check success, cancellation or error feedback. Previewing does not confirm settlement.",5:"If amounts are wrong, inspect the settlement’s sources and saved payment records. Receivables come from admitted checklists and valid quotation facts, paid amounts come from settlement payment records, and remaining amounts are calculated from settlement data. Do not type a substitute amount into a template."},result:"The template controls presentation. Actual amounts and status come from settlement records. Confirmed or frozen settlements continue to use protected historical content; editing a template does not settle them again.",notes:{1:"This article covers templates. Settlement confirmation, payment changes and reversals require their own permissions and business conditions; template editing cannot bypass them.",2:"Customer settlement output and internal cost Excel are separate. Costs, suppliers and profit must stay out of customer documents. Internal cost output additionally requires sensitive-cost access.",3:"An unsaved payment draft is not evidence of a saved paid amount. Default-template or layout edits must not silently rewrite frozen settlements or their source history."}},"cost-analysis-template":{purpose:"Maintain internal cost-analysis Excel workbooks for checklist and project settlement cost review.",entry:"System Settings → Templates & Assets → Template Settings, then Excel Templates → Cost analysis Excel. Run actual cost exports from the checklist or settlement page.",prerequisites:"Template upload and maintenance require the corresponding permissions; cost review and output require sensitive-cost access. Prepare a standard, unencrypted .xlsx workbook.",steps:{1:"Select Cost analysis Excel and inspect system and user templates. System or read-only templates cannot be directly replaced; maintain your own workbook for changes. Legacy settlement cost templates, if shown, are historical references; current settlement cost analysis reuses the cost-analysis template.",2:"Download the marker sample and build a workbook using its available fields. Supported content includes project, customer, quote tracing and amount summaries, plus product and adjustment loops. Internal fields can include cost price, supplier, product cost, profit and margins.",3:"Use the sample’s markers, which stand for fields, in cells. Follow its loop start, prototype-row and end structure. Use supported fields only; do not invent nested loops or unknown markers. The sample explains syntax rather than providing a finished business template.",4:"Enter a name and upload the .xlsx. Check the target before replacing an existing user template. Only validated files are usable. For failures, check the format, field spelling, uniformly formatted complete markers and loop placement, then correct and retry.",5:"Use the list to download the current file, re-validate, enable or disable, and set a default. Generation uses the default, or the most recently updated enabled template when there is no default. Return to internal cost output in a checklist or settlement and check real data and the save result."},result:"The usable workbook renders internal cost Excel through supported fields and loops. It does not change cost calculations or settlement records.",notes:{1:"Cost analysis and customer quotation Excel are separate types. Costs, profits and suppliers are internal information for authorized staff and must not be sent as a customer quote. Customer quotation templates reject sensitive-cost markers.",2:"Failed validation is not a successful import. Do not rename the extension, ignore errors or bypass validation. Correct unreadable, encrypted or unsupported workbooks in spreadsheet software first.",3:"The current sample and validation feedback define supported capabilities. Arbitrary macros, complex loops and advanced layouts are not guaranteed. Enabled and default states control later output selection; they do not prove historical files or other devices have updated."}},"cloud-local-only-mode":{purpose:"Understand local workspaces and Team collaboration, and respond to visible sync and connection states.",entry:"System Settings → Data & Storage → Cloud & Local Mode. Administrators configure Cloud here; members use the Team entry offered during setup or sign-in to join an existing Team.",prerequisites:"Identify the workspace and current identity first. Cloud management requires the relevant settings permission; provider setup and high-risk local unbinding additionally depend on local administrator and session checks. A local role cannot replace Team identity.",steps:{1:"In local-only use, permitted modules support projects, checklists, quotations, customers, products, fulfillment and settlement. Local-first means valid actions are saved on the device first. It does not mean they have uploaded, or that every action is permitted offline.",2:"An authorized administrator uses the existing connection wizard to create or reconnect a Team Cloud workspace and follows its checks. Handle sensitive configuration only within the protected dedicated flow. Keep keys, passwords, Team connection credentials and debugging content out of help requests, screenshots and articles.",3:"After configuration, inspect initial-sync readiness. Cloud connection and first business sync are separate: Team identity, settings and permissions precede structured business data, followed by file resources. Structured readiness does not mean every attachment or font can already be opened on this device.",4:"Members use the administrator-provided Team join method and authenticate on the protected page. Check the actual Team, member identity and accessible projects. The local user list is not the Team directory; joining does not make an ordinary member the owner.",5:"For daily work, inspect sync state, pending changes and prompts. Syncing means processing continues. Waiting can mean dependencies or resources are not ready. Preserve work while offline and check convergence after reconnecting. Use the offered sign-in entry when reauthentication is required; inspect the relevant item for errors or attention requests.",6:"Use manual sync, pause or resume when offered. Ordinary network loss is not a reason for immediate unbinding. Repair, leaving Cloud and stale-binding recovery must use an available entry with its preflight, identity checks and warnings. Preserve data and contact an administrator when uncertain."},result:"Check local saves, Team authority, server acknowledgement and file availability separately. Treat each part as synchronized only when its state and actual records confirm it.",notes:{1:"Cross-device updates of system settings and custom Team roles are confirmed by the actual result on member devices. An administrator’s local save does not confirm member convergence. Concurrent edits may require conflict handling; the last local save cannot be assumed to overwrite every device.",2:"Retire this cloud connection under Manage cloud connection is a high-risk action that appears only when the page’s eligibility conditions are met. It requires the confirmation text and the current local system administrator password (not the cloud workspace administrator password). It only detaches this computer from the current cloud connection: local business data is kept, and existing spaces and data in the old cloud are not deleted automatically. Pending changes not yet uploaded through the old connection are not migrated or uploaded to the old cloud after retirement. This is not ordinary reconnection. Members should involve an administrator, never manually clear bindings.",3:"Team collaboration requires the current identity, connection status and sync readiness checks to pass before the corresponding Team capabilities can be used. When the page shows not ready, needs attention or sign-in required, follow its prompt first and do not assume Team data is available.",4:"Data sync and file sync are different. Signing out is not safely leaving a Team. Do not create a replacement Cloud workspace, import an old backup or reset local data to bypass sync errors."}},"backup-restore-later":{purpose:"Save the local workspace through system backups and understand controlled recovery capabilities and risks.",entry:"System Settings → Data & Storage → Backup & Restore. First-run setup may also offer backup recovery; follow the entries shown by the current client.",prerequisites:"The corresponding management permission and supported desktop backup or recovery capability are required, with no blocking recovery state. Destructive local restore additionally requires verified local-only authority; Cloud-managed workspaces cannot use it.",steps:{1:"Save current business edits and check the workspace and materials to retain. Choose a backup type: Basic Backup supports safety archiving and checks but cannot directly restore the entire workspace; System Backup preserves system state for complete local restore; Full Backup retains project materials and business files more comprehensively.",2:"Choose the create-backup action, wait for preparation and integrity checks, and select a save location in the system dialog. Do not repeatedly create while processing. Judge the result by included content and completion feedback rather than file size alone.",3:"Check completion, filename, size and integrity feedback, then keep the file safely. Cancelling the save is cancellation; for failure, inspect the reported file or storage condition. Neither means backup success. The page’s current-session result is not a complete backup-history manager.",4:"Before restoring, assess the risk of replacing current data and confirm local-only workspace conditions. Choose Restore from backup. In the controlled recovery interface, select the file and inspect compatibility, backup type and restorability first. Legacy or Basic backups may support inspection without full restore.",5:"Only when validation passes and restore is permitted, read the warnings and confirmation carefully, proceed through the controlled flow and wait for explicit completion. Restore replaces current local state; preserve current data first and never use it to overwrite an online Team directly.",6:"For cancellation, failure or failed validation, stop and keep the original file. Record the page’s non-sensitive error description. Do not edit backup internals, rename extensions or bypass checks. Without completion feedback, do not assume restore succeeded."},result:"A successful backup has a saved file and completion feedback. Successful restore must be confirmed by the separate recovery flow; opening recovery or selecting a file does not mean data was restored.",notes:{1:"Web/PWA does not provide the full recovery capability of a supported Native desktop client. For unavailable controls, check the environment, permission and page hints. Recovery capability is determined by the actual page in a supported desktop client.",2:"Restore is not ordinary template import. Format, version and current-client compatibility must pass validation. Even System or Full backups are not guaranteed to restore on every version.",3:"A Cloud workspace may allow backup inspection, but Cloud Restore is currently unavailable. Local recovery cannot obtain or replace Team authority, or directly overwrite an existing Cloud workspace with old data. Ask an administrator to handle binding barriers through controlled workflows.",4:"Restore is high risk; cancellation is not success. Treat data as restored only after the recovery flow explicitly reports completion."}}},Xct={articles:Yct,center:{search:"Search help articles",searchPlaceholder:"Search titles, steps or tips",navigation:"Help categories and articles",empty:"No matching articles. Try another search term.",back:"Back to article list",onThisPage:"On this page",related:"Related help",clearSearch:"Clear search",articleCount:"Articles: {count}",resultCount:"Matching articles: {count}",selectedHidden:"The article you are reading is not in the current results.",purpose:"What this helps with",entry:"Where to start",prerequisites:"Before you begin",steps:"Steps",result:"After completion",notes:"Limits and tips"},categories:{gettingStarted:"Getting started",projects:"Projects and Project Flow",commercial:"Quotes and commercial work",operations:"Fulfillment and after-sales",settings:"Configuration and permissions"},topics:{"product-library-basics":{title:"Product Library basics",summary:"Manage products by brand and model, and distinguish current costs from historical snapshots."},"customer-library-basics":{title:"Customer Library basics",summary:"Maintain customers and contacts, bind projects and review applicable quotation history."},"app-basics-navigation":{title:"App navigation and workspace",summary:"Find modules and projects, and understand saving, returning and narrow-screen use."},"formal-quote-and-signing":{title:"Formal quotations and signing",summary:"Understand formal revisions, QVS1, quoted status and signing order."},"project-lifecycle":{title:"Projects and Project Flow basics",summary:"Create a project, explore its home page and distinguish progress tracking from business actions."},"setup-wizard-overview":{title:"First setup and workspace entry",summary:"Choose local setup, team entry or backup recovery and understand workspace readiness."},"role-permission-defaults":{title:"Roles and Permissions",summary:"Configure capabilities and distinguish project scope, local identity and Team authority."},"checklist-config-fields":{title:"Checklist field configuration",summary:"Configure field availability, workspace display and customer quotation visibility."},"cost-adjustment-config":{title:"Cost adjustment configuration",summary:"Maintain amount and percentage adjustments, permissions and historical amount boundaries."},"project-flow-template":{title:"Project Flow Templates and Configuration",summary:"Maintain default stages, tasks and categories while protecting existing project history."},"quote-template-editor":{title:"Quotation Template Management",summary:"Manage customer quotation designs and distinguish formal revisions from Excel workbooks."},"settlement-template":{title:"Settlement Template Management",summary:"Configure settlement layouts and fields, with clear amount sources and historical protection."},"cost-analysis-template":{title:"Cost Analysis Templates",summary:"Upload and validate internal cost Excel templates, then manage enabled and default states."},"shipment-rules":{title:"Orders, shipments and receipts",summary:"Order and ship remaining quantities in batches, forward stored goods and confirm receipt."},"recycle-library-rules":{title:"Product returns and recycling",summary:"Check return sources and process recycle inbound, stock actions and reuse."},"after-sales-rules":{title:"After-sales checklists and operations",summary:"Create and confirm after-sales work, distinguishing output, fulfillment, returns and settlement."},"cloud-local-only-mode":{title:"Local Workspace and Team Cloud Sync",summary:"Understand local-first work, Team entry, sync states and the conditions for controlled recovery."},"backup-restore-later":{title:"Data Backup and Restore",summary:"Choose backup types, check saved results and understand controlled desktop recovery limits."}}},$ct={notice:{title:"Diagnostics Center",description:"Generate a bounded, read-only support snapshot without business payloads, file bytes or credentials. Engineering-only command checks remain separately gated."},snapshot:{title:"Support diagnostics snapshot",description:"A local, provider-neutral summary for support conversations. It can be generated while offline and never changes sync, binding or business data.",refresh:"Generate / refresh snapshot",refreshing:"Generating…",copy:"Copy diagnostics",export:"Export diagnostics",actionCompleted:"Completed",actionFailed:"Failed",failed:"One or more diagnostic sources were unavailable; the remaining safe sections are still available.",loading:"Generating a read-only snapshot…",generatedAt:"Generated at",client:"Client",displayIdentity:"Display identity",desktopInternalBuild:"Desktop